<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20061] Add an option to hide/show root in lfs quota -a output</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20061</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;lfs quota -a is a useful option for printing quota settings and usage status for all users, groups, and project IDs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;# lfs quota -a -u /exafs/
Disk usr quotas
      Filesystem  quota_id  kbytes   bquota  blimit  bgrace   files   iquota  ilimit  igrace
         /exafs/      root 92192924        0       0       -    2223        0       0       -
         /exafs/      1000       0        0 1073741824       -       0        0       0       -
         /exafs/      1001       0        0 2147483648       -       0        0       0       -
         /exafs/      1002       0        0 3221225472       -       0        0       0       - &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However, in many cases, users want to ignore the quota information for root, since it is usually not relevant for quota administration and makes the output noisier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It would be helpful to add an option to control whether the root entry is shown.&lt;br/&gt;
also It's better if root is hidden by default and would add an option to show full prints?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
